lity replication constitutes a harm that copyright's existing doctrinal scope cannot reach, requiring a compensatory mechanism beyond traditional infringement remedies.\n\nThe concrete proposal: a fund financed by a flat percentage of AI service revenue, administered by an independent body with small-creator representation, distributing based on cryptographic provenance logs weighted by corpus share and model revenue, with sector-level displacement adjustments for professions where aggregate capability replication devalues entire fields even absent verbatim copying. The auditor body operates under the Skeptic's four conditions. Private discovery survives as a failsafe. If this framework is rejected in favor of pure sector-level displacement metrics with no input-level measurement, the result is a fund that compensates creators for harm without any structural connection to the training decisions that caused it — a severance package with no accountability for the firing.",
